    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d185">

                <pb facs="0324" n="225" xml:id="pg225"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.00/752: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Muccio</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-05-17T12:00:00-04:00">May 17, 1936—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received
                        4:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>21. My telegram of May 16, 7 p.m.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d185-f1"/> President
                    resigned 2 a.m. Manifesto issued by Acting Chief General Staff<anchor n="7"
                        xml:id="d185-f2"/> this morning states army assumes supreme mandate not to
                    possess itself of the political power but to restore order. Army to associate
                    itself with the more popular political parties to select a mixed junta.
                    Manifesto states provisional government will respect and faithfully comply with
                    all treaties and accept international pacts.</p>
                <p>Meeting of army, Socialists and Republican Socialists leaders now in progress in
                    Government Palace awaiting instructions from Colonel Toro still in Villa
                    Montes.</p>
                <p>La Paz exceptionally quiet with soldiers patrolling streets. No information is at
                    hand from outlying centers.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Muccio</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
